      </table>
    </div>

    <p>
      Genre selection strongly impacts sales performance. Games built around deep systems and mechanical replayability tend to earn higher median revenues than simple platforming games.
    </p>

    <!-- Table 2: Genre Performance -->
    <div class="table-wrapper">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Genre Category</th>
            <th>Median Gross Revenue (100+ Reviews)</th>
            <th>Market Characteristics</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Factory / Automation</strong></td>
            <td>$200,000 – $500,000+</td>
            <td>Strong player demand, deep systems, lower competition</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Colony Simulator</strong></td>
            <td>$100,000 – $300,000</td>
            <td>High average playtime, loyal fanbase</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Roguelite / Survival</strong></td>
